  "complete_source_ending": "The first contour measured a derivative which vanished with constant weight. The three-boundary K3 experiment distinguished two products on which every specified trace agreed. The sourced neutral disk can be distinguished from the vacuum even though they have the same total charge, and its entire normalized law still leaves the absolute vacuum amplitude free. In each case a boundary calculation acquires its force from knowing which insertion was made, which operation was kept, and which states it can distinguish. For connected ordered coefficients there is a theorem that the cuts suffice. For the level-one disk one can give the independent preparations and compare them on every harmonic coordinate. For a gravitational filling the action, the states it can prepare, and the amplitude of a cut must all be identified in the same theory. That is what it would mean to recover an interior from its boundary.",
